Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         proxmox-ve (>= 8.0) | pve-manager (>= 8.0),
         open-iscsi,
         multipath-tools,
         libwww-perl,
         liblwp-protocol-https-perl,
         libxml-libxml-perl
Recommends: sg3-utils, psmisc, lsscsi
Description: QNAP NAS storage plugin for Proxmox VE
 A Proxmox VE custom storage plugin for QNAP QTS and QuTS hero over iSCSI, in
 which one VM disk is one thin LUN on the NAS, so the NAS's own snapshots and
 clones act on the unit an operator thinks about — no LVM layer and no shared
 LUN carved up locally.
 .
 Registers the storage type "qnapsan". It requires Storage Manager V2, which
 QTS 4.5.1 and every QuTS hero provide; the plugin refuses a firmware that
 reports the legacy Storage Manager rather than failing later.
 .
 Every 0.x release is a prerelease. Nothing array-facing has run against a NAS
 yet; what has and has not been
 exercised against real hardware is listed in
 /usr/share/doc/jt-pve-storage-qnap/TESTING.md. Read it before putting data on
 this.
 .
 Two things shape what this plugin can offer. It does not set up per-host
 access lists on the target, so CHAP is the access control it relies on. And QTS
 allocates LUNs in whole GiB, so every disk size is rounded up.
 .
 This is an independent project. It is not developed, certified, endorsed or
 maintained by QNAP Systems, Inc.
 .
 Also ships pve-qnap-api-probe, a read-only tool that asks a NAS what it
 supports, and pve-qnap-reap, which clears leftovers a node keeps after a VM is
 migrated away.
 .
 The plugin must be installed on every node of the cluster.
